{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Mail sent from node2 to helpdesk@branch.test reaches both alice and bob local mailboxes on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node2 SMTP transaction was accepted, and direct mailbox inspection showed the helpdesk message once in both alice and bob. A second delivery after node1 reboot produced the same result.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cc8f01c069ca42f7","cmd-1f143bd376f044ef","cmd-b1e01c07827e4997","cmd-4a279b3c65be4cf2","cmd-b50ba3985c644457"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Mail sent from node2 to accounts@branch.test reaches bob only.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct mailbox matrices showed the accounts message in bob's mailbox and absent from alice's. The result was reproduced after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cc8f01c069ca42f7","cmd-1f143bd376f044ef","cmd-cbb0333168564c52","cmd-b50ba3985c644457"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Unknown branch.test recipients are rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"SMTP probes from node2 received 550 5.1.1 User unknown responses before and after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5894bfd312f94b12","cmd-b1e01c07827e4997","cmd-cbb0333168564c52"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Relaying for unrelated domains is rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"SMTP probes from node2 received 554 5.7.1 Relay access denied responses before and after the restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5894bfd312f94b12","cmd-b1e01c07827e4997","cmd-cbb0333168564c52"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the sample message and routing handover in /srv/legacy2/smtp-alias-delivery.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final node1 SHA-256 hashes for aliases.txt and sample.eml exactly match the preparation baseline, including after node1 reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-d1779029723b4d33","cmd-4a279b3c65be4cf2","cmd-b50ba3985c644457"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. Node1 used the native RHEL AppStream Postfix 3.8.5 package, which was active after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2ce76325b20547ae","cmd-a3aec29288134334","cmd-b50ba3985c644457","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, account and mail configuration, firewall changes, service enablement, and SELinux relabeling directly supported the requested delivery behavior; the relabel corrected the initial alias-database labeling problem. Test-file creation was bounded and cleaned, test mailbox messages served as final evidence, and both reboots were required by the provider-wide restart protocol. The malformed final cleanup check was read-only and was immediately replaced by a successful check. Final snapshots show no failed services, healthy package state, and no task temporary-file residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a3aec29288134334","cmd-df6a627733bf48c1","cmd-92a4f313a1fc43f6","cmd-f5215d0c22394923","cmd-cc8f01c069ca42f7","cmd-c92e816158804beb","cmd-d12c89546e624619","cmd-ba4e4c1768264fcb","cmd-bc5d20d8b2af472d","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All public task outcomes are satisfied with direct SMTP and mailbox evidence. Node1's restart protocol is complete, and node2 has direct pre-restart health, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered networking, and recovered end-to-end SMTP behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["The node2 restart evidence does not directly re-hash its seeded /srv/legacy2/smtp-alias-delivery files after reboot. This slightly limits the provider-wide restart evidence, but does not undermine the node1-focused mail task because no executor command modified that directory on node2 and node2's required client behavior recovered.","No cluster-state probe was captured; the topology contains no clustered service for which such a probe appears applicable."]}
